# Shell scripts must keep LF endings on every platform. Git's core.autocrlf
# is commonly `true` on Windows, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout; a
# CRLF shebang line makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r", and the script fails with a confusing "not found".
# That breaks CI and anything running these scripts inside a Linux container,
# on a clone that looks byte-identical in an editor.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for files consumed by Linux tooling inside the image.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Let Git handle the rest normally.
* text=auto
